From: jaydens-tasty-slop
 <325336397+jaydens-tasty-slop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 07:49:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] utils/orientationsensor: Keep the last reading when
 subscribing again

Auto-rotation unsubscribes from the orientation sensor while the
screen is off. When the screen turns back on, subscribe() reports the
reading of the new subscription straight away, but that reading is
always Undefined: the ClaimAccelerometer() and Get() calls have not
been answered yet. An Undefined reading applies the manual transform,
so on a tablet held in landscape whose manual transform is portrait
the output turns to portrait on every wake and back to landscape about
a second later, when the real reading arrives.

Keep the last known orientation until the subscription has a reading.
The Qt Sensors based implementation behaved like this too: the reading
it went back to after start() was the last one the sensor had.

Still report the first reading of a new subscription when it matches the
last known one, so the outputs are put back to the sensor orientation if
they were reconfigured while the screen was off, as they were before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UQSvSLBoFcFR7i6bQghXDu
---
 src/utils/orientationsensor.cpp | 19 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/utils/orientationsensor.cpp b/src/utils/orientationsensor.cpp
index fe4cbb5..83b8457 100644
--- a/src/utils/orientationsensor.cpp
+++ b/src/utils/orientationsensor.cpp
@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@
 #include <QDBusPendingCall>
 #include <QDBusServiceWatcher>
 
+#include <utility>
+
 namespace KWin
 {
 
@@ -208,11 +210,20 @@ void OrientationSensor::subscribe()
     }
 
     m_subscription = std::make_unique<OrientationSensorSubscription>();
-    connect(m_subscription.get(), &OrientationSensorSubscription::readingChanged, this, [this]() {
-        updateOrientation(m_subscription->reading());
+    // A new subscription has no reading until net.hadess.SensorProxy answers.
+    // Keep the last known orientation until then, rather than reporting it as
+    // undefined, which would rotate the output to its manual transform and
+    // back every time the screen turns on.
+    connect(m_subscription.get(), &OrientationSensorSubscription::readingChanged, this, [this, firstReading = true]() mutable {
+        const AccelerometerOrientation reading = m_subscription->reading();
+        if (std::exchange(firstReading, false) && reading == m_orientation) {
+            // The outputs may have been reconfigured while there was no
+            // subscription, so report the first reading even if it's unchanged.
+            Q_EMIT readingReceived();
+        } else {
+            updateOrientation(reading);
+        }
     });
-
-    updateOrientation(m_subscription->reading());
 }
 
 void OrientationSensor::unsubscribe()
